|term[description]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss A predicate the world satisfies; picks out whatever currently satisfies it — plurality is a feature.
  :dual-of @designator
  |designation description
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-descriptors
    :anchor descriptor-kinds
    :projection paraphrase
    A predicate the world satisfies: nothing was ever bound; the connection is re-computed, every time it is used, from whatever currently satisfies the predicate.
  |formal
    :notation <latex:refs(desc, t) = \{ x \mid P(x) \; at \; t \}>
    :reading The referent set is a function of the evaluation moment; zero, one, or many.
  |set-rel :kind subset-of :to @descriptor
  |set-rel :kind disjoint-from :to @designator
  |invariant
    Kind is per-act (descriptor's [[DECISIONS#d12-location-is-description|D12 location-is-description]] theorem); the location family is the OWNED description — its container's community can enumerate and route it, which free predicates cannot claim.
  |note :audience maintainer
    Steward skepticism recorded (def-descriptors WN): "silent re-satisfaction" as this kind's failure mode may be state-based cruft an event-sourced foundation dissolves; adjudication deferred to the Temporal chapter.
